## Root cause

The harness compile gate (`longrun/bin/dispatch_loop.py::compile_gate`) does **not** run inside `release/` — it walks the whole worktree and runs:

```bash
lake env lean <absolute path to each .lean file>   # cwd = worktree root
```

But the D6 scaffold keeps `lakefile.toml`, `lean-toolchain`, and `.lake` under `release/`, and the longrun elan installation has no default toolchain. So every invocation aborted *before elaboration*:

```
error: no default toolchain configured. run `elan default stable` ...
```

I reproduced this exactly (exit 1 on `GibbsSharp.lean` from the worktree root). The gate's `gate.json` had already been deleted by the dispatcher when it queued the repair, so I re-derived the failure from the dispatcher source and re-ran the commands.

## Fix (no mathematical file touched)

Added four root-level shims so the gate's cwd is a valid Lake workspace that re-exposes the prebuilt tree:

| Shim | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `lean-toolchain` | pins `leanprover/lean4:v4.34.0-rc2` at the gate's cwd |
| `lakefile.toml` | root package, `packagesDir = ".lake/packages"`, mathlib require |
| `lake-manifest.json` | byte copy of `release/lake-manifest.json` (offline resolution) |
| `.lake -> release/.lake` | re-exposes prebuilt `Poincare` oleans and `packages/` |

